WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.702 --> 00:00:05.092
Welcome to Bravo K9 transport tracking.
This guide

2
00:00:05.092 --> 00:00:07.217
shows you how to open the vehicle map,

3
00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.806
check its last update, and find your
private

4
00:00:09.806 --> 00:00:13.959
trip information. Then, we’ll cover the
sharing checklist

5
00:00:13.959 --> 00:00:17.840
for the Bravo team. Watch, pause, and
follow

6
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.867
along.

7
00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:23.644
Visit bravo unleashed dot com on your
phone,

8
00:00:23.694 --> 00:00:27.381
tablet, or computer. Open the menu and
choose

9
00:00:27.381 --> 00:00:31.457
Track Bravo, Glympse. You can also open
K9

10
00:00:31.457 --> 00:00:35.415
Transport and select Track the Bravo
vehicle. Both

11
00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:39.283
routes take you to the same tracking
section.

12
00:00:40.285 --> 00:00:42.668
Select View vehicle map to load the
Glympse

13
00:00:42.668 --> 00:00:46.056
viewer inside the website. You do not
need

14
00:00:46.056 --> 00:00:49.157
to install the Glympse app just to watch.

15
00:00:49.207 --> 00:00:51.954
For a larger view, select Open Glympse
full

16
00:00:51.954 --> 00:00:55.483
screen. That opens the shared vehicle
map in

17
00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:57.950
a separate tab.

18
00:00:58.952 --> 00:01:01.882
Look for the last-update time inside
Glympse before

19
00:01:01.882 --> 00:01:05.191
relying on the marker. An old position
can

20
00:01:05.191 --> 00:01:09.475
remain visible after sharing pauses or
expires. A

21
00:01:09.475 --> 00:01:11.532
marker on the map does not always
mean

22
00:01:11.532 --> 00:01:14.566
the vehicle is moving right now. Check
your

23
00:01:14.566 --> 00:01:18.033
trip notes for arrival updates.

24
00:01:19.035 --> 00:01:22.605
Choose Copy tracking link. Then paste it
into

25
00:01:22.605 --> 00:01:24.780
a text message or save it somewhere
easy

26
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.074
to find. Copying does not send a
message

27
00:01:28.074 --> 00:01:32.019
for you. If automatic copying is blocked,
select

28
00:01:32.019 --> 00:01:35.589
and copy the link shown on screen.
Remember,

29
00:01:35.639 --> 00:01:37.735
anyone with this link can view the public

30
00:01:37.735 --> 00:01:40.117
vehicle map.

31
00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:44.153
For your dog’s transport details, open
the Breeder

32
00:01:44.153 --> 00:01:46.158
and Client Portal and sign in with your

33
00:01:46.158 --> 00:01:49.662
own Bravo account. You’ll see trips Bravo
has

34
00:01:49.662 --> 00:01:52.605
assigned to you. The public map and
your

35
00:01:52.605 --> 00:01:56.199
private trip details are separate. If your
trip

36
00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:58.803
is missing, contact Bravo so the team
can

37
00:01:58.803 --> 00:02:01.450
check your access.

38
00:02:02.452 --> 00:02:04.197
If the map is blank or looks out

39
00:02:04.197 --> 00:02:06.853
of date, try Open Glympse full screen
and

40
00:02:06.853 --> 00:02:10.436
check the last-update time again.
Sharing may have

41
00:02:10.436 --> 00:02:13.144
expired, or the vehicle’s phone may have
lost

42
00:02:13.144 --> 00:02:17.545
signal. Check your private journey notes.
If you

43
00:02:17.545 --> 00:02:20.071
still need an update, call Bravo using the

44
00:02:20.071 --> 00:02:22.825
website’s phone link.

45
00:02:23.827 --> 00:02:26.774
The next steps are for the Bravo team.

46
00:02:26.824 --> 00:02:29.246
Location sharing starts in the Glympse
app on

47
00:02:29.246 --> 00:02:32.423
the phone traveling with the vehicle.
Opening the

48
00:02:32.423 --> 00:02:36.238
website does not turn tracking on. Set
everything

49
00:02:36.238 --> 00:02:39.975
up while parked, before the journey
begins. App

50
00:02:39.975 --> 00:02:43.325
screens can vary by version.

51
00:02:44.327 --> 00:02:47.335
Open Glympse and select the Bravo K9
Transport

52
00:02:47.335 --> 00:02:51.204
tag, spelled exactly as shown on screen.
If

53
00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.691
you are creating a new share, choose
Share

54
00:02:53.691 --> 00:02:57.053
Location and add the tag as a recipient.

55
00:02:57.103 --> 00:02:59.863
Set the sharing duration, then send or
start

56
00:02:59.863 --> 00:03:02.949
the share. Open the viewer and confirm
the

57
00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:06.242
marker has a recent update.

58
00:03:07.244 --> 00:03:09.861
At a safe stop, check the phone’s battery,

59
00:03:09.861 --> 00:03:14.147
connection, and remaining sharing time.
Extend the active

60
00:03:14.147 --> 00:03:16.842
share, or restart sharing to the same tag

61
00:03:16.842 --> 00:03:20.241
if it has expired. In Bravo, use the

62
00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:22.988
trip editor for care notes and revised
arrival

63
00:03:22.988 --> 00:03:27.116
estimates. Quick care buttons prepare a
draft; review

64
00:03:27.116 --> 00:03:30.075
it and save the update.

65
00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.176
After a handoff, mark the appropriate
trip delivered

66
00:03:34.176 --> 00:03:37.577
in Bravo. When the vehicle’s transport
run is

67
00:03:37.577 --> 00:03:40.220
finished, open the active share in
Glympse and

68
00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:44.074
stop sharing. Marking a trip delivered,
hiding the

69
00:03:44.074 --> 00:03:46.808
website map, or closing the browser
does not

70
00:03:46.808 --> 00:03:50.575
stop the phone’s public location share.

71
00:03:51.577 --> 00:03:54.860
Clients: open the map, check the
last-update time,

72
00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.968
and use your own account for private
trip

73
00:03:56.968 --> 00:04:01.879
details. Bravo team: start, maintain, and
stop sharing

74
00:04:01.879 --> 00:04:04.834
in the Glympse app. Keep dog names
and

75
00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:08.936
customer addresses out of public tag
messages. Bravo

76
00:04:08.936 --> 00:04:16.533
K9 Solutions. Trust. Train. Deploy.
